menu "MagTag Timer"

    config MAGTAG_SYNC_LED_FEEDBACK
        bool "NeoPixel feedback during NTP sync"
        default y
        help
            Show blue on the NeoPixels while WiFi is up and SNTP sync is in
            progress, and blink red three times if the sync fails. Useful
            during bring-up/debugging; disable for production builds
            (CONFIG_MAGTAG_SYNC_LED_FEEDBACK=n in sdkconfig.defaults).

    config MAGTAG_PARENT_TESTING
        bool "Button B manually resets the timer"
        default y
        help
            Testing convenience: Button B resets the timer to IDLE with the
            full daily allocation. Disable for production builds so the
            allocation only resets on day rollover — otherwise the timer's
            user could refund their own screen time.

    config MAGTAG_WEEKDAY_MIN
        int "Weekday screen-time allocation (minutes)"
        default 60
        range 1 1440
        help
            Daily allocation on weekdays. Seeds NVS; changing this (or any
            allocation) reseeds NVS defaults on the next boot automatically
            (the stored stamp is a fingerprint of these values).

    config MAGTAG_WEEKEND_MIN
        int "Weekend screen-time allocation (minutes)"
        default 120
        range 1 1440
        help
            Daily allocation on Saturdays and Sundays.

    config MAGTAG_HOLIDAY_MIN
        int "Holiday screen-time allocation (minutes)"
        default 120
        range 1 1440
        help
            Daily allocation on dates in the NVS holiday list.

    config MAGTAG_BREAK_INTERVAL_MIN
        int "Eye-rest break interval (minutes of running time)"
        default 30
        range 0 480
        help
            After this many minutes of accumulated RUNNING time, the timer
            auto-pauses into an enforced Screen Break. 0 disables eye-rest
            breaks entirely.

    config MAGTAG_BREAK_DURATION_MIN
        int "Eye-rest break duration (minutes)"
        default 15
        range 1 120
        help
            Length of the enforced Screen Break. When it ends the device
            chimes and waits in PAUSED for a manual resume (Button A).

    config MAGTAG_IDLE_SYNC_INTERVAL_MIN
        int "NTP sync interval while IDLE (minutes)"
        default 60
        range 5 1440
        help
            How often the clock re-syncs while the timer is IDLE. The
            ESP32-S2 has no crystal-backed RTC — deep-sleep timekeeping
            runs on an RC oscillator that can drift minutes per day, so
            long intervals make the displayed clock visibly wrong.
            RUNNING keeps its own fixed 10-minute cadence.

    config MAGTAG_QUIET_START_HHMM
        int "NeoPixel quiet hours start (HHMM, 24h)"
        default 2230
        range 0 2359
        help
            Status NeoPixels (state pixel, WiFi sync feedback) stay dark
            from this local time until the quiet-hours end. Encoded as
            HHMM: 2230 = 10:30 PM. Set start == end to disable quiet
            hours. Alert pulses (expiry) are NOT suppressed — they
            accompany an audible alarm and are dismissable.

    config MAGTAG_QUIET_END_HHMM
        int "NeoPixel quiet hours end (HHMM, 24h)"
        default 800
        range 0 2359
        help
            Local time the status NeoPixels come back. 800 = 8:00 AM. A
            window with start > end wraps midnight.

endmenu
